      "noteEn": "As a noun, químicos names people who work in chemistry. The same form can mean “chemical” when it describes masculine plural things.",
      "example": { "es": "Los químicos comprobaron la reacción.", "en": "The chemists checked the reaction." },
      "tags": ["word", "profession", "chemistry", "plural"]
    },
    {
      "id": "phrase-ordenar-por-criterio",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "ordenar algo por + criterio",
      "questionEn": "How do you say what criterion is used to order or rank a set of things?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of ordenar, then por before the criterion used for the order.",
      "noteEn": "The things can come first when ordenado functions as a description: libros ordenados por autor. Ordenado changes to match them: ordenada, ordenados, or ordenadas.",
      "example": { "es": "La lista está ordenada por fecha.", "en": "The list is ordered by date." },
      "tags": ["phrase", "ordering", "por", "criterion", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar-estar-bien-infinitive-evaluation",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "estar bien + acción en forma de diccionario",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that doing something is good, fine, or acceptable?",
      "answerEn": "Use está bien, then put the action verb in its unchanged dictionary form.",
      "noteEn": "This is a general evaluation, so Spanish does not need a separate subject meaning “it.” The action remains in the form ending in -ar, -er, or -ir: está bien preguntar, aprender, or salir.",
      "example": { "es": "Está bien cambiar de opinión.", "en": "It is fine to change your mind." },
      "tags": ["grammar", "evaluation", "estar bien", "infinitive", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "concept-academic-fields-purity-hierarchy",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "campos ordenados por pureza · ciencias aplicadas · matemáticas",
      "answerEn": "the comic ranks academic fields by how abstract or theoretical they appear",
      "noteEn": "Each field dismisses the one to its left as merely an applied form of itself. Mathematics is drawn farthest from practical application, which makes the distance itself part of the joke.",
      "tags": ["concept", "academic fields", "purity", "hierarchy", "xkcd"]
    }
